AB  - In adaptive AR storytelling, many systems still rely on coarse object labels and fixed spatial anchors, treating environments as static backdrops and overlooking semantic depth in how objects relate. We present an object-driven AR story framework that integrates Vision-Language Models (VLMs) with a mediating layer we call Spatial-Object Semantics, allowing nuanced narrative cues aligned with the scene in real time. Experimental results show that guiding VLMs with appropriate layered semantics transforms AR scenes from static settings into dynamic, story-rich spaces, coordinating perception, context, and plot while preserving real-time responsiveness, marking a step toward more expressive, responsive AR narratives.
