AB  - Traditional Air Traffic Management (ATM) simulations are constrained by time-intensive setups, manual configurations, and limited accessibility for non-technical stakeholders during scenario generation. To overcome these challenges, we present a Mixed Reality (MR) Digital Twin Platform for ATM using HoloLens 2 enabling Natural Language Processing (NLP) with Large Language Models (LLMs) for real-time scenario generation, allowing access directly to multiple stakeholders including non-technical participants to add aircraft, adjust taxi routes, or simulate emergencies and non-nominal events during simulation runtime through natural language commands. By minimizing reliance on scripted pre-designed files, the platform significantly reduces setup times and development cycles, simplifying advanced Mixed Reality scenario generation and customization. In addition, dynamic taxi route management and real-time pathfinding enhance adaptability to various operational requirements for aircraft movement. This approach bridges the gap between technical developers and operational users, making ATM simulations more flexible, accessible, and efficient for a wide range of stakeholders.
