AB  - Reminiscence is the activity of recalling and revisiting a memory. Past research highlights that reminiscence in older adults can promote healthy aging, improve psychological well-being, and could foster inter-generational communication. Virtual reality offers benefits to reminiscence as it allows users to reenact the past in embodied, immersive, and multi-sensory ways. A key challenge in VR reminiscence is the recreation of past scenes that are relevant and familiar to each user. Thus, this research seeks to evaluate and implement GenAI to prototype 360-degree scenes based on inputs that are relevant to each user. In particular, we examine the implementation 1) text-to-image and 2) panorama outpainting generation methods for 360-degree scenes. This study aims to bring personalization and control to the recreation of memories in VR. Moreover, this work strives to support the democratization of content creation in VR for users with various degrees of technical expertise.
